 "etapas": [
  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Nominalising in a formal style",
     "texto": [
      "**A/V-(으)ㅁ** turns an action or quality into a noun: after a vowel or ㄹ, **-ㅁ** is added (가다 → **감**, 살다 → **삶**); after other consonants, **-음** (먹다 → **먹음**, 좋다 → **좋음**). In notices, reports and notes it can present a fact concisely.",
      "행사 일정이 **변경되었음을 알려 드립니다** = we inform you that the event programme has been changed."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Use and reading",
     "texto": [
      "In this register, **-았/었음** can close a statement as a note or a fact. With nouns, **N(이)다 → N임**: 신청 기간은 10월 20일까지**임** = the registration period is until 20 October. It is not automatically replaced by **것** in every sentence; you have to recognise the notice format."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
